  "worked_solution": "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[-1,1),$ the interval from $-1$ to $1$ (including $-1$ but not including $1$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is ${-1,1},$ the set containing the two numbers $-1$ and $1$ only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
